lls/120746","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3497693523"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120746#discussion_r3497693523"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120746"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3497693523/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":150,"original_line":150,"side":"LEFT","in_reply_to_id":3494668112,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":4,"position":4,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3497711935","pull_request_review_id":4599151486,"id":3497711935,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc7Qetk_","diff_hunk":"@@ -379,7 +379,7 @@ class Image : public Resource {\n \t// Returns true when the image is empty (0,0) in size.\n \tbool is_empty() const;\n \n-\tVector<uint8_t> get_data() const;\n+\tconst Vector<uint8_t> &get_data() const _LIFETIME_BOUND_;","path":"core/io/image.h","commit_id":"0a50997da81144f13ed7a4eeedc22b90c1ef98ac","original_commit_id":"b148cb42a5314e317622168e5562191818bf0a9d","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Just to double check before approval (as this change to accessors is the most controversial in the PR), is there any possibility that the previous version might have provided some kind of COW like protection of the internal `Vector<uint8_t>` being changed while the client still had their own `Vector`?\r\n\r\ni.e. Is it always a good idea for us to return const reference instead of e.g. `const Vector<uint8_t>`? ","created_at":"2026-06-30T09:39:22Z","updated_at":"2026-06-30T09:39:59Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120746#discussion_r3497711935","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120746","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3497711935"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120746#discussion_r3497711935"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120746"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3497711935/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":382,"original_line":382,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3494620404,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":5,"position":5,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3497752843","pull_request_review_id":4599198264,"id":3497752843,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc7Qe3kL","diff_hunk":"@@ -379,7 +379,7 @@ class Image : public Resource {\n \t// Returns true when the image is empty (0,0) in size.\n \tbool is_empty() const;\n \n-\tVector<uint8_t> get_data() const;\n+\tconst Vector<uint8_t> &get_data() const _LIFETIME_BOUND_;","path":"core/io/image.h","commit_id":"0a50997da81144f13ed7a4eeedc22b90c1ef98ac","original_commit_id":"b148cb42a5314e317622168e5562191818bf0a9d","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Since it's returned as `const`, it's immune to tinkering (unless illegally `const_cast`). \r\n\r\n> i.e. Is it always a good idea for us to return const reference instead of e.g. const Vector<uint8_t>?\r\n\r\nI would say so. Returning a copy unnecessarily bumps the refcount too.\r\nTwo situations that speak against it:\r\n\r\n- If you don't want to expose what data format you store (keep the door open for synthesizing it). In most cases this is a bad idea because requiring conversion on access could be a performance footgun.\r\n- If the data is likely to internally mutate, so your const ref might not be stable. Though in practice you can just make a copy, and this is a risk present all throughout c++, so returning a copy just for that is premature optimization.\r\n\r\nSo yea, in practice, I would always return a const ref instead of a copy.","created_at":"2026-06-30T09:46:11Z","updated_at":"2026-06-30T09:46:24Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120746#discussion_r3497752843","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120746","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3497752843"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120746#discussion_r3497752843"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120746"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3497752843/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":382,"original_line":382,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":3494620404,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":5,"position":5,"subject_type":"line"}]